{"id":"000VMP","title":"Degrees of Disorder","author":"dawsonjones2020","solvedCount":0,"difficulty":4,"rating":"N/A","firstSeen":"2026-10-20T22:21:36+00:00","posted":"Gestern, 22:54 Uhr","rules":"I’ve previously made a couple of chaos construction puzzles where circled digits counted the region-border edges around their cells. Those puzzles received mixed reviews, but solving a few recent slitherlink puzzles inspired me to revisit the idea - this time counting the eight surrounding dots touched by region boundaries instead. I think this ruleset leads to some interesting new logic. Hope you enjoy!\n\nSolve on SudokuPad\n\nRules\n\nChaos Construction: Divide the grid into nine orthogonally connected regions of nine cells. Each row, column and region contains the digits 1–9 once each.\n\nGlobal Entropy: Every 2×2 contains at least one digit from each group: 1–3, 4–6 and 7–9.\n\nCircles: Every cell is surrounded by eight dots. A digit in a circle indicates how many of its cell’s dots lie on a region boundary. The outer border of the grid counts as a region boundary. Count each dot once, even if multiple boundaries meet there.\n\nBlack Kropki: If two digits are joined by a black dot, one is double the other.","solutionCode":"The lengths of the continuous groups of cells belonging to the same region in column 7, from top to bottom. Enter a new number whenever a region border is crossed.","tags":["Sudoku"],"links":[{"url":"https://sudokupad.app/lgimwygojn","kind":"sudokupad"}],"data":"","error":null,"settings":{},"link":"https://sudokupad.app/lgimwygojn","linkKind":"sudokupad","summary":{"format":"scl","decoded":true,"rows":9,"cols":9,"cages":0,"hasSolution":true,"features":["underlays"]},"attempts":0,"fetched":"2026-10-20T22:21:36+00:00"}